The implementation of the nsIDOMHTMLAppletElement interface creates a JS wrapped Java applet object, whose prototype is an HTMLAppletElementInstance. Inside the various DOMIDL generated method implementations, there is a code sequence:

nsIDOMElement *nativeThis = (nsIDOMElement*)JS_GetPrivate(cx, obj);

This is incorrect when the actual object is a wrapped (by LiveConnect) Java object. We need to use the new tag bit that indicates when private data is actually an nsISupports* of some kind. I've added a new static method to nsJSUtils:

nsISupports* nsGetNativeThis(JSContext *cx, JSObject *obj);

This walks the prototype chain of the object, and returns the first object that is marked as having both private data and an nsISupports* stored in the private data. The DOMIDL compiler should be revised to generate:


T *nativeThis = (T*)nsJSUtils::nsGetNativeThis(cx, obj);®

