document.open();
document.clear();
... do stuff ...
document.close();

is a common idiom in pre 5.0 releases.  In this release, document.clear() does
not yet exist.  At a minimum, it should exist and simply do nothing before
returning.  A better choice would be to see if the document has any content and
remove it if there is any.

