I am trying to write some code that sets the blur string for the AutoComplete
Widget (ACW) used in the messenger compose window. Whenever a user types
something, the ACW displays a colored, non-selectable, non-editable string (blur
string) to the right of what he typed that represents the ACW's best guess.

I am trying to use the ":after" pseudo element to implement the blur string:

<html>
<head>
<style>
body:after {
             content: "@netscape.com <No Match>";
             color:   blue;
           }
</style>
</head><body>kin</body></html>


I have some code that uses the nsDOMCSSStyleDeclaration methods to change the
"content:" property:



    nsCOMPtr<nsIDOMCSSStyleDeclaration> declaration;

    ...

    result = declaration->SetProperty("content", "@foo.com <Blur Test>", "");



But it doesn't cause the screen to update with my new "content:" property value
because nsCSSFrameConstructor::StyleRuleChanged() doesn't Remap the style
context before reconstructing the frames with ReconstructDocElementHierarchy(),
so the old context string is always re-rendered.

I'm forced to work around the problem by setting some other propery like
"color:" that forces a remap, and then resetting the "content:" property to
force a re-framing:



    result = declaration->SetProperty("content", "@foo.com <Blur Test>", "");
    result = declaration->SetProperty("color", "red", "");
    result = declaration->SetProperty("content", "@foo.com <Blur Test>", "");

